  "sentences": [
    {
      "start": 0.8,
      "end": 3.9,
      "text": "Two bakers opened their shops on the same street."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.15,
      "end": 6.9,
      "text": "Both started with exactly six hundred dollars."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.2,
      "end": 9.3,
      "text": "Both spent their money making bread."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.6,
      "end": 14.5,
      "text": "And by the end of the day, both had sold one thousand dollars' worth of bread."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.4,
      "end": 18,
      "text": "But the next morning, something strange happened."
    },
    {
      "start": 18.35,
      "end": 20.65,
      "text": "One baker opened his shop like usual."
    },
    {
      "start": 21,
      "end": 24.1,
      "text": "The other couldn't even afford to buy flour."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.4,
      "end": 25.6,
      "text": "Here's what happened."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.5,
      "end": 29.9,
      "text": "The first baker sold his bread directly to customers."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.1,
      "end": 32.1,
      "text": "Every customer paid him immediately."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.4,
      "end": 37.1,
      "text": "So by the end of the day, he had one thousand dollars in cash."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.5,
      "end": 41.2,
      "text": "He used six hundred dollars to prepare the next batch."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.7,
      "end": 44.1,
      "text": "And the business kept running."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.3,
      "end": 47.7,
      "text": "But the second baker did something different."
    },
    {
      "start": 48,
      "end": 52.3,
      "text": "Instead of selling to customers, he sold all his bread to a supermarket."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.6,
      "end": 56.1,
      "text": "The supermarket agreed to pay him one thousand dollars..."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.2,
      "end": 58.6,
      "text": "Sixty days later."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.2,
      "end": 60.55,
      "text": "Now think about that."
    },
    {
      "start": 60.8,
      "end": 62.85,
      "text": "Both bakers made the same sales."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.1,
      "end": 67.05,
      "text": "Both had four hundred dollars in gross profit, before other expenses."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.3,
      "end": 69.7,
      "text": "But one had a thousand dollars in cash."
    },
    {
      "start": 70,
      "end": 72.5,
      "text": "And the other had a thousand dollars on paper."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.75,
      "end": 75.1,
      "text": "He had to wait sixty days to collect it."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.25,
      "end": 78,
      "text": "And without additional cash, he couldn't afford to make another batch."
    },
    {
      "start": 78.7,
      "end": 83.2,
      "text": "You see, making a profit and having cash are two different things."
    },
    {
      "start": 83.6,
      "end": 88.4,
      "text": "Because a business can look profitable on paper... and still run out of money."
    }
  ],
